      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To find the product of the roots of the polynomial equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots.\n\nFor a polynomial of the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\), Vieta's formulas tell us:\n1. The sum of the roots (\\(\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma\\)) is equal to \\(-\\frac{b}{a}\\).\n2. The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time (\\(\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha\\)) is equal to \\(\\frac{c}{a}\\).\n3. The product of the roots (\\(\\alpha\\beta\\gamma\\)) is equal to \\(-\\frac{d}{a}\\).\n\nFor the polynomial \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\), we have \\(a = 3\\), \\(b = -1\\), \\(c = -20\\), and \\(d = 27\\). Applying Vieta's formulas, we get:\n1. The sum of the roots \\(\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = -\\frac{-1}{3} = \\frac{1}{3}\\).\n2. The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time \\(\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = \\frac{-20}{3}\\).\n3. The product of the roots \\(\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = -\\frac{27}{3} = -9\\).\n\nThe product of the roots is \\(-9\\). Let's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\n# Coefficients of the polynomial 3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27\na = 3\nb = -1\nc = -20\nd = 27\n\n# Using Vieta's formulas\nproduct_of_roots = -d / a\nprint(product_of_roots)\n```\n```output\n-9.0\n```\nThe product of the roots of the equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\) is \\(\\boxed{-9}\\).",
