      "text": "To find the product of the roots of the polynomial equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. For a cubic equation of the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\), Vieta's formulas tell us that the product of the roots is given by \\(-\\frac{d}{a}\\).\n\nIn our equation, \\(a = 3\\) and \\(d = 27\\). Therefore, the product of the roots is:\n\\[\n-\\frac{27}{3} = -9\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code. We'll use numerical methods to find the roots of the polynomial and then compute their product.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\n# Coefficients of the polynomial 3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27\r\ncoefficients = [3, -1, -20, 27]\r\n\r\n# Find the roots of the polynomial\r\nroots = np.roots(coefficients)\r\n\r\n# Calculate the product of the roots\r\nproduct_of_roots = np.prod(roots)\r\nprint(product_of_roots)\n```\n```output\n-9.000000000000002\n```\nThe product of the roots of the equation \\(3x^3 - x^2 - 20x + 27 = 0\\) is \\(\\boxed{-9}\\).",
